the US Federal Reserve's long  anticipated move was a vote of  confidence in the American economy and  its recovery from the Great Recession of  2008-2009 it also recognizes the  considerable progress that has been made  toward restoring jobs raising incomes  and easing the economic hardship of  millions of Americans and it reflects  the committee's confidence that the  economy will continue to strengthen the  economic recovery has clearly come a  long way although it is not yet complete  muted reaction was felt on global  markets in New York the Dow Industrials  closed one and a quarter percent higher  stocks made modest gains across Asia as  well with japan's nikkei average closing  one-point-six percent higher and hong  kong's hang seng index up eight tenths  of a percent it already is put you know  raising the dollar and therefore putting  downward pressure on emerging market  currencies although I think other  factors are even more important I think  for example the rebalancing in China  away from importing commodities is  having a bigger effect on an emerging  markets by far and causing their  currencies to go down and weakening  their exports overall the feds move is  being seen as a positive for the world  economy a strengthening US economy  should help boost demand for commodities  and industrial goods worldwide
 

